### 3. Synergy Realization Principle (2 + 2 = 5)

The frameworks detail the drivers for value creation post-transaction[cite: 1]:

| Synergy Type | Classification | Key Drivers & Examples |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Cost Synergies**[cite: 1] | Hard Synergies (Tangible cost savings)[cite: 1] | Eliminating overlaps in **Staffing** (HR/Legal/Finance), **Facilities**, **Procurement** bulk discounts, and unifying **IT Systems**[cite: 1]. <br> *Case Studies:* Exxon & Mobil (1999), Tata Steel & Corus (2007)[cite: 1]. |
| **Revenue Synergies**[cite: 1] | Soft Synergies (Top-line revenue expansion)[cite: 1] | **Cross-Selling**, expanding geographic distribution, **R&D Innovation**, and leveraging **Brand Power**[cite: 1]. <br> *Case Study:* Disney acquiring Pixar (2006)[cite: 1]. |

